      "name": "GPIO23",
      "label": "GPIO23 (Button)",
      "codeName": "23",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_input",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "BOOTSEL / user button — not declared in this board's pins_arduino.h (no PIN_BUTTON alias), but confirmed via the official Pimoroni datasheet's pinout diagram ('BOOTSEL GP23 — BOOT/DFU mode protected by diode', distinct from the separate RESET->RUN hardware-reset button) and product-page text ('Switch for basic input (doubles up as DFU select on boot)'; 'clever circuitry that lets you use the boot button as a user controllable switch'). digital_output/pwm_output deliberately omitted — no vendor source confirms driving this diode-coupled BOOT/DFU line as an output is safe; matches the conservative precedent set for u-blox EVK-NORA-W10 GPIO0 (SW2/BOOTn) in variants/esp32/esp32s3/nora_w10/board.json.\nCheck if available on board"
    },
